%% This diagram is the evaluation methodology for the matched DEV/TEST workbench (the four
%% systems: hybrid, legal_static, planned_multisearch, adaptive) -- not a script or a command
%% to run. It shows three separate, parallel judging tracks that every scenario goes through,
%% and why: bundle sufficiency (does the combined evidence satisfy the private, held-back
%% requirements -- with adjudication when judges disagree), answer-generation correctness
%% (checked against independently-verified source excerpts), and pooled passage relevance
%% (nDCG/diagnostics, pooling every system's retrieved passages together before judging, so no
%% single system's own output defines what counts as relevant). The dotted line at the bottom
%% is the key safeguard: the private requirements are never supplied to the system being
%% evaluated while it runs -- only used afterward, by the judges. See TECHNICAL_APPENDIX.md
%% section 4.0, "Evaluation methodology, and what you need before running any of it", for how
%% this maps to the actual runnable commands (prw run / prw pool / prw judge / prw judge-bundles
%% / prw judge-answers / prw evaluate) and for the prerequisite: a working retrieval index, OR
%% just the already-shipped results/runs/*.jsonl files -- no rebuild required either way.
flowchart TD
    A[Public source-guided scenario] --> B[Static retrieval or bounded controller]
    B --> C[Same final K and text budget]
    D[Private evaluator requirements] --> E[Three blinded bundle judges]
    C --> E
    E --> F{Material disagreement?}
    F -->|yes| G[Independent adjudication]
    F -->|no| H[Silver bundle sufficiency]
    G --> H
    C --> I[Same answer generator]
    I --> J[Three blinded answer judges]
    K[Verified independent source excerpts] --> J
    C --> L[Union of all systems' passages]
    L --> M[Three blinded passage judges]
    M --> N[Pooled nDCG and pointwise diagnostics]
    H --> O[Paired scenario-level results and cost]
    J --> O
    N --> O
    D -. never supplied .-> X[Runtime controller has no answer key]
